{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2021-06-25 08:30:00', 'title': 'ABBVIE PROVIDES UPDATE REGARDING RINVOQ® (UPADACITINIB) IN PSORIATIC ARTHRITIS AND ANKYLOSING SPONDYLITIS IN THE U.S.', 'text': 'NORTH CHICAGO, ILL., JUNE 25, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- ABBVIE (NYSE: ABBV) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT THE U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA) HAS INFORMED THE COMPANY THAT THE FDA WILL NOT MEET THE PRESCRIPTION DRUG USER FEE ACT (PDUFA) ACTION DATES FOR THE SUPPLEMENTAL NEW DRUG APPLICATIONS (SNDAS) FOR RINVOQ® (UPADACITINIB) FOR THE TREATMENT OF ADULTS WITH ACTIVE PSORIATIC ARTHRITIS AND ADULTS WITH ACTIVE ANKYLOSING SPONDYLITIS.'}
{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2021-06-25 02:30:00', 'title': 'CHMP RECOMMENDS APPROVAL OF RINVOQ® (UPADACITINIB) FOR THE TREATMENT OF ATOPIC DERMATITIS', 'text': "NORTH CHICAGO, ILL., JUNE 25, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- ABBVIE (NYSE: ABBV) TODAY ANNOUNCED THE EUROPEAN MEDICINES AGENCY'S (EMA) COMMITTEE FOR MEDICINAL PRODUCTS FOR HUMAN USE (CHMP) ADOPTED A POSITIVE OPINION RECOMMENDING THE APPROVAL OF RINVOQ® (UPADACITINIB), AN ORAL, SELECTIVE AND REVERSIBLE JAK INHIBITOR, FOR THE EXPANDED USE IN ADULTS (15 MG OR 30 MG, ONCE DAILY) AND ADOLESCENTS 12 YEARS AND OLDER (15 MG, ONCE DAILY) WITH MODERATE TO SEVERE ATOPIC DERMATITIS WHO ARE CANDIDATES FOR SYSTEMIC THERAPY."}